ion; post-restart boot_id (15ef0089...) differs from pre-restart, matching the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot; sshd, the certificate, and sshd_config directive were confirmed intact, and a fresh CA-trust-only client reconnected successfully post-restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d5852c63725a4116\",\"cmd-1d783349502143e4\",\"cmd-19623e787e524983\",\"cmd-032da80685e043a1\",\"cmd-0c669255ac524c70\",\"cmd-325d33c685e84cdc\",\"cmd-36e995337e9040fe\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map cleanly to the task or the restart protocol: CA generation, host-cert signing, sshd_config edit, sshd reload, and the pre/post-restart reboot itself are all justified and left in an intact, non-conflicting final state (confirmed by the after_executor snapshot showing no failed services, consistent listening sockets, and a matching new boot_id). Temporary client key/known_hosts files created for the CA-trust verification test were removed (cmd-5963e2ce568f468a partially failed on one file due to permission, corrected immediately by cmd-56ab7d2c8c014f88 as root), and the post-restart test client files were cleaned up inline in cmd-36e995337e9040fe. The one unresolved item is cmd-e2496d62ba6c44d9, which appended CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY as a second key in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on node1 to enable the client-side verification test; this key was never removed and persists as residue after task completion, a bounded but retained credential addition not required by the certificate-authority task itself.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e2496d62ba6c44d9\",\"cmd-5963e2ce568f468a\",\"cmd-56ab7d2c8c014f88\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created an SSH host CA on node1, signed the ed25519 host key as a host certificate, configured and 